  "grammar": [
    {
      "id": "b1_u02_l1_g1",
      "pattern": "연음 (bog'lanib o'qish)",
      "meaning_uz": "받침 keyingi unliga o'tib o'qiladi",
      "meaning_en": "Linking: a final consonant moves to the next vowel",
      "explanation_md": "Bo'g'in **받침** bilan tugasa va keyingi bo'g'in **ㅇ + unli** bilan boshlansa, 받침 **keyingi bo'g'inga o'tib** o'qiladi. Yozuv o'zgarmaydi — faqat talaffuz.\n\n- **음악** → [**으막**]\n- **한국어** → [**한구거**]\n- **이름이** → [**이르미**]\n- **옷이** → [**오시**]\n\n### Nega muhim\n\nKoreyslar so'zlarni bog'lab gapiradi. **일요일**ni [이료일] deb eshitasiz. Eshitganingizni yozganda asl yozuvni eslang: [한구거] emas, **한국어**.\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- **ㅇ** bo'g'in boshida tovushsiz — shuning uchun 받침 shu bo'sh joyga \"ko'chadi\".\n- **ㅎ** 받침 tushib qoladi: **좋아요** → [**조아요**].\n- Ikki 받침li so'zlarda (읽어요) biri o'tadi: [**일거요**].",
      "explanation_md_en": "When a syllable **ends in 받침** and the next one **starts with ㅇ + vowel**, the 받침 **moves over** to the next syllable. The spelling stays the same — only the sound changes.\n\n- **음악** → [**으막**]\n- **한국어** → [**한구거**]\n- **이름이** → [**이르미**]\n- **옷이** → [**오시**]\n\n### Why it matters\n\nKoreans link words as they speak. You'll hear **일요일** as [이료일]. When you write what you hear, remember the real spelling: **한국어**, not [한구거].\n\n### Remember\n\n- **ㅇ** is silent at the start of a syllable, so the 받침 \"moves into\" that empty slot.\n- A **ㅎ** 받침 disappears: **좋아요** → [**조아요**].\n- With a double 받침 (읽어요), one consonant moves: [**일거요**].",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "받침 + ㅇ",
          "condition_en": "받침 + ㅇ",
          "rule": "받침 → keyingi bo'g'in",
          "example": "음악 [으막], 한국어 [한구거]"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "ㅎ 받침 + ㅇ",
          "condition_en": "ㅎ 받침 + ㅇ",
          "rule": "ㅎ tushadi",
          "example": "좋아요 [조아요]"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Ikki 받침",
          "condition_en": "Double 받침",
          "rule": "ikkinchisi o'tadi",
          "example": "읽어요 [일거요]"
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "ko": "음악을 들어요. [으마글 드러요]",
          "uz": "Musiqa tinglayman.",
          "en": "I listen to music.",
          "audio": "e962922b7e32.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "한국어를 배워요. [한구거를 배워요]",
